 Each guide takes a sheet on the night: the walk's heading, then one line per booking so they can tick people off at the start.
 
+## Waiting list
+
+The council's street-performance licence allows 20 people on a walk, not counting the guide. Bookings are confirmed first come, first served, and a party is never split. Once a party doesn't fit, it and every booking taken after it go on the waiting list in booking order, so nobody jumps the queue, even a smaller party that would fit. The guide rings the waiting list if anyone doesn't turn up.
+
+The limit is the licence's, not ours: Bethan agrees any change with the council's licensing team, and it goes in this README before the code changes.
+
 ## Usage
 
 ```
